  "geometry_source_note": "Latest 2026-09-23 front/rear static linkage tables supersede all member endpoint coordinates, including rod endpoints. Table inches map to model (X,Y,-Z), with no additional rear offset. Shock endpoints and rocker pivot centers retain preceding millimeter screenshots. Rocker rod joints follow new inboard rod points; assumed planar pivot axes recomputed. Sources: examples/sources/mk12_linkage_table_updates_2026-09-23.json and mk12_rocker_updates_2026-09-23.json. Left side mirrored from right.",
  "load_case_note": "Opposite-direction acceleration/cornering and braking/cornering cases swap left/right wheel force vectors and negate their lateral component. Longitudinal and vertical components are retained from the opposite wheel, preserving mirrored load transfer. Both turn directions contribute to all sizing envelopes."
